--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT THE WEB PAGE IS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
QuietHoursPage.tsx is the dedicated /notifications/quiet-hours wrapper. It is a
thin composition surface: it renders a PageContainer (title, subtitle, copyLink)
and stacks two already-built shared surfaces —
  <AIQuietHoursSuggestion onApplyDraft={handleApplyDraft} />
  <QuietHoursPanel seedDraft={pendingSeed} onSeedConsumed={handleSeedConsumed} />
The page owns ONE piece of state: useState<QuietHoursWindowInput | null>
(pendingSeed). The AI advisor proposes a window; handleApplyDraft stores it as
pendingSeed; QuietHoursPanel consumes it as a one-shot create-form seed and fires
handleSeedConsumed, which clears the pointer back to null. The advisor is
propose-only (ADR-015 §I8) — the panel keeps the sole canonical Save button.
No API feed is fetched by the page itself; the manifest declares the unit as
scaffold-only (requiredCount=2: notifications.quietHours.title + .subtitle).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NATIVE IMPLEMENTATION (no placeholders, ADR-011; no delegation)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Both shared A3 surfaces already exist and own their own data states, so they are
embedded verbatim, never re-implemented (DRY, ADR-006) — the same pattern the
sibling TeslaRegionPage / GasPriceAutoPollPage wrappers use to host their shared
feature view:

  - io.teslasync.android.featureviews.quiethourspanel.QuietHoursPanel
      Owns the windows feed (cache-then-network) + every state: loading skeleton,
      empty state, hard-error+retry, stale-offline, content; the inline
      create/edit form; the per-window rows; the toast queue; the canonical Save.
      Accepts seedDraft + onSeedConsumed.
  - io.teslasync.android.sharedsurfaces.aiquiethourssuggestion.AIQuietHoursSuggestion
      Owns the AI draft stream (resting / loading / content / empty / error /
      rate-limit / stale-offline), the captured-proposal preview, and the
      per-feature AI-Off gate (renders nothing when closed — web withAiFeature).
      Accepts onApplyDraft.

This page is their notifications host: it renders the PageContainer-equivalent
header, stacks the two surfaces in the web page's order, and owns the pending-seed
hand-off between them (the verbatim native port of the web useState + handlers).

New files (package io.teslasync.android.notifications.quiethours):
